
Welcome to Cameo — any AMD card -> a working LLM box.

  This box does not need the internet to serve.
  Network is for extra models, other Cameo nodes, and the console
  from outside the house.

  cameo gpu-status              your GPU's support tier (1/2/3)
  cameo serve qwen2.5-0.5b      starter model — already on disk, no network
  cameo pull --list             more aliases, if you want the network
  cameo --help                  everything else

A starter GGUF (qwen2.5-0.5b) is already in /var/lib/cameo/models.
Open the web console printed on first boot and chat. Extra models: drop a
.gguf there, or `cameo pull` when you have a network.

Running from the USB? Install to this machine's disk (offline, copies the image):
  cameo-install-guided   the installer — account, disk, confirm
  cameo-install          dry run — shows the plan, changes nothing

Docs & source: https://github.com/sadlowskik/Cameo
